# Database — regenerate with: python -m backend.scripts.seed
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Model artifacts — regenerate with: python -m backend.ml.train
# Includes holdout_ids.json, which is derived from the seed and so is
# reproducible on any machine that runs seed.py with the same fixed RNG seed.
backend/ml/artifacts/
*.joblib
*.pkl

# Cached threat-intel feeds — repopulate with: python backend/scripts/fetch_feeds.py
# Not committed because they are large, they go stale, and CISA KEV is public
# anyway. The system degrades gracefully when the cache is missing.
backend/app/data/feeds/
data/training.csv
*.csv.gz

# Secrets
*.key

# Server logs
*.log

# Planning and internal briefs — local only.
# api-contract.md, backend-contract.md and STATE.md ARE shared: they are the
# two team seams plus the handoff doc, and the project is unworkable without
# them. PLAN.md and the frontend/demo-site briefs were scaffolding.
PLAN.md
RUNBOOK.md
docs/*
!docs/api-contract.md
!docs/backend-contract.md
!docs/STATE.md

